    {
      "id": "u04-3",
      "title": "My name is…",
      "explanation": [
        "**My naam is …** = My name is … .",
        "**Wat is jou naam?** = What is your name? (**wat** = what)",
        "**u** is the polite *you*. Use it with older people and strangers: **Wat is u naam?**",
        "Older people are often called **Oom** (uncle) and **Tannie** (auntie), even if they aren't family. It's a sign of respect.",
        "**Aangename kennis!** = Pleased to meet you!"
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "af": "My naam is Anna.",
          "en": "My name is Anna."
        },
        {
          "af": "Wat is jou naam?",
          "en": "What is your name?"
        },
        {
          "af": "Goeie môre, Oom. Hoe gaan dit met u?",
          "en": "Good morning, sir. How are you?"
        },
        {
          "af": "Aangename kennis!",
          "en": "Pleased to meet you!"
        }
      ],
